  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A compass needle of oscillation magnetometer oscillates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> times per minute at a place <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> of dip <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The number of oscillations per minute become <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> at another place <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;dip. The ratio of the total magnetic field at the two places <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>At point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;the needle oscillates&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;times per minute. Therefore, time period&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;and at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p><p>The time period of oscillation magnetometer is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>I</mi><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>I</mi><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mi>cos</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>I</mi><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mi>cos</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Taking ratio,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
